-- title:
--   Idempotents lift along 𝔪 B for finite algebras over henselian local rings
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a henselian local ring, and let $B$ be a commutative $R$-algebra that is finite as an $R$-module. Write $\mathfrak m \subseteq R$ for the maximal ideal of $R$ and let $\mathfrak m B =$ `Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R)` denote the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m$ under the structure map $R \to B$. The assertion is that for every element $e_0$ of the quotient ring $B/\mathfrak m B$ satisfying $e_0^2 = e_0$ there exists $e \in B$ with $e^2 = e$ whose class under the quotient map $B \to B/\mathfrak m B$ is $e_0$. Only existence of a lift is asserted; no uniqueness statement is made, and no restriction (such as reducedness, or $\mathfrak m B$ being nilpotent) is placed on $B$ beyond module-finiteness over $R$. Note that $R$ and $B$ are allowed to lie in different universes.
--
--   This is one of the standard characterisations of henselian local rings: idempotents of the reduction modulo the maximal ideal of a finite algebra lift, which amounts to saying that a finite algebra over a henselian local ring decomposes as a finite product of local rings. It is used here to produce idempotents, hence clopen decompositions, in the proof that clopen subsets of the special fibre of a proper scheme over a henselian local ring come from clopen subsets of the whole space ([`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClopen_preimage_eq_of_isProper_of_henselianLocalRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClopen_preimage_eq_of_isProper_of_henselianLocalRing)); the proof goes through the lifting property of henselian local rings for étale algebras, [`HenselianLocalRing.exists_algHom_lift_of_etale`](thm.html#HenselianLocalRing.exists_algHom_lift_of_etale).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HenselianLocalRing_exists_isIdempotentElem_map_eq_of_module_finite.lean

import Mathlib

